 ${misc:Depends},
Recommends:
 postgresql,
Description: self-hosted error tracking and performance monitoring
 Tindra is self-hosted error tracking, performance, uptime and cron
 monitoring that works with Sentry SDKs. It runs as one binary with one
 PostgreSQL database and serves its web UI itself.
 .
 debconf asks for the public URL, sets up a local PostgreSQL database and
 creates the first account; dpkg-reconfigure tindra changes the settings
 later. Configuration is in /etc/tindra/tindra.env, data in /var/lib/tindra.
